---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="16 August 2026"
  summary="This site is static. It has no accounts, no login, no database, and no analytics. The short version: we do not collect anything about you."
>
  <section>
    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing. There is no sign-up, no contact form, no comment box, no
      newsletter, no shopping cart, and no analytics script. We do not set any
      cookies and we do not use local storage. No profile of you is created,
      because nothing is recorded to create one from.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third parties that do see something</h2>
    <p>
      Two parties observe the request that loads this page. Neither is under our
      control, and both are named here so nothing is hidden:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-mist-200">Netlify</strong> hosts the site. Like any
        web host, its servers process your IP address and browser user-agent in
        order to send you the page, and it keeps standard access logs. See the
        <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" rel="noopener"
          >Netlify privacy policy</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-mist-200">Google Fonts</strong> serves the three
        typefaces this page uses. Your browser requests them from Google's
        servers, which means Google receives your IP address when the page
        loads. See the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener"
          >Google privacy policy</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you would rather not have that font request happen at all, the fonts can
      be self-hosted so the page makes zero third-party requests. This is a known
      concern under the GDPR and is a change we will make on request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Links away from this site</h2>
    <p>
      This page links to GitHub and to the upstream Langfuse project. Once you
      follow one of those links you are on someone else's site, under their
      privacy policy, not this one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The software is separate from this website</h2>
    <p>
      This policy covers the website only. muxaris is self-hosted software that
      runs on your own infrastructure. It sends no telemetry to us, and we have
      no visibility into your deployment, your prompts, your model traffic, or
      your API keys. Whatever your installation does with data is governed by
      your own systems and by the terms of whichever model providers you point it
      at.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Rights such as access, correction, deletion and portability apply to
      personal data a controller holds about you. We hold none, so there is
      nothing to retrieve or erase. If you believe otherwise, open an issue on
      the repository and we will look into it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this site ever starts collecting something — analytics, an email list,
      accounts — this page will be updated before that goes live, and the "last
      updated" date above will change.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
